### File 5 — MODIFY `resource/scss/components/_button.scss`

Append after the final `.no-prev-button` block (after line 518). The existing file ends at line 518 with no trailing newline issue — append directly:

```scss
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// no-btn-char — per-character rolling text button
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.no-btn-char {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: fluid(6, 10);
  text-decoration: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  font-family: var(--family-ui);
  color: inherit;

  // --- size modifiers -------------------------------------------------------

  &--sm {
    @include font("f-body-3");
  }

  &--md {
    @include font("f-body-2");
  }

  &--lg {
    @include font("f-body-1");
  }

  // --- text wrapper: clips each rolling cell --------------------------------

  &__text {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  // --- one cell per character -----------------------------------------------

  &__cell {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    // height comes from line-height of the font; do not set explicitly
    display: inline-block;
  }

  // --- both char slots share base styles ------------------------------------

  &__char {
    display: inline-block;
    will-change: transform;

    &--orig {
      // default — in view; GSAP moves to yPercent: -100 on hover
    }

    &--clone {
      // sits below the cell at rest; GSAP pulls to yPercent: 0 on hover
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      transform: translateY(100%);
    }
  }

  // --- icon (base) ----------------------------------------------------------

  &__icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: fluid(12, 14);
  }

  // --- icon-reveal modifier: hidden → visible on hover, CSS-only -----------

  &__icon--reveal {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateX(-4px);
    transition:
      opacity var(--transition-fast),
      transform var(--transition-fast);
  }

  &:hover &__icon--reveal,
  &:focus-visible &__icon--reveal {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateX(0);
  }

  // --- reduced motion override ----------------------------------------------

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    &__char--orig,
    &__char--clone {
      will-change: auto;
      transition: none;
    }

    // Prevent GSAP from visually animating — the JS still fires but GSAP
    // respects this via the CSS property check; for hard safety we also
    // keep the chars at their resting positions via inline reset in JS.
    // Icon reveal is also simplified:
    &__icon--reveal {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }
  }
}
```

**`prefers-reduced-motion` note**: GSAP 3 honours `prefers-reduced-motion` automatically when the `ReducedMotion` plugin is registered. For safety without depending on that plugin, `will-change: auto` and the CSS reset on `--orig` / `--clone` positions are set. If GSAP still fires (it will complete instantly), the user sees no perceptible animation.

---

### Integration Notes

#### `killTweensOf` optionality

The real `GsapGlobal` in the codebase (line 131 of `gsap.types.ts`) has `killTweensOf?` marked optional. The component uses `gsap.killTweensOf?.(...)` optional-chaining throughout, which is correct. The prompt's stub marks it non-optional — the actual codebase takes precedence.

#### `overwrite` property on GSAP vars

`overwrite: "auto"` is passed inside the `vars` object (`gsap.to(target, vars)`). Since the method signature is `to(target: unknown, vars: object): unknown`, TypeScript accepts any `object` literal here — no type widening issues.

#### `for...of` string iteration for Korean characters

Korean Hangul syllable blocks (e.g. `무`) are single code points and single UTF-16 code units, so `split("")` would also work, but `for...of` is the correct approach for full Unicode correctness (surrogate pairs in emoji) and matches the intent.

#### Stagger on array targets

Passing `this._origChars` (an `HTMLElement[]`) as the first argument to `gsap.to` is valid — GSAP accepts arrays. The `stagger` property inside vars applies the per-element delay.

---

